// Heading-hold profile behind models/heading_hold/skill_heading_hold_goal3_alpha_guard.mpk —
// the first heading_hold checkpoint retrained after the 2026-08-06 physics/envelope changes
// (training integrator 60 -> 64 Hz, target-airspeed floor 110 -> 90 m/s), which left every
// earlier checkpoint behaviorally stale. NOT the task default; pass explicitly via
// --reward-config.
//
// Differs from heading_hold_ultra_tight_tracking.reward.ron (its direct ancestor, values
// otherwise unchanged) only by turning ON the angle-of-attack margin guard:
//
//     alpha_soft_limit: 0.25, alpha_excess_scale: 0.05, alpha_excess_weight: 1.0
//
// Why the guard exists. The generic jet stalls at alpha = (cl_max - cl0)/cl_alpha = 0.289 rad
// (16.6 deg). At the low-speed/high-altitude corner the airspeed floor opened up (90 m/s at
// 5000 m, 7000 kg loaded) level flight already needs CL ~= 1.15 of the 1.4 available, so
// sustained level turns are bank-limited to ~35 deg and there is almost no maneuvering margin.
// Nothing in the pre-guard reward kept a policy off cl_max — `compute_aero_forces` just clamps
// CL, so a policy that keeps pulling for altitude or turn rate mushes and departs rather than
// getting a gradient telling it not to. Live-sim (Rapier) rollouts of every pre-guard candidate
// departed at 5000 m / 90 m/s / 120 deg turn with alpha pegged past 40 deg; the bank_excess term
// does not catch this, because bank is not what stalls the airframe.
//
// 1000-episode eval at the full 500:5000 m / 90:140 m/s / -180:180 deg envelope:
//   success_rate = 0.995, mean_tail_abs_heading_rad = 0.008559 (0.49 deg),
//   mean_tail_abs_altitude_m = 1.431, mean_tail_abs_speed_mps = 0.323.
// Live Rapier check at four nominal operating points (1000 m/100, 3000 m/120, 800 m/140,
// 2000 m/110, turns of +90/180/+45/-90 deg): altitude 0.97-1.58 m, airspeed 0.37-0.39 m/s,
// heading 0.31-0.51 deg. Known limit: the extreme corner (>=5000 m AND <=90 m/s AND a large
// commanded turn) still departs — the PID expert loses ~111 m of altitude at that same point
// (examples/heading_hold_expert_baseline.rs), so it is an airframe-margin corner, not a
// tracking-quality one. Do not chase it by loosening max_altitude_error.
//
// Recipe (each stage 4M steps, --target-speed-range 90:140, --target-alt-range 500:5000,
// starting from the 2026-08-06 tier-2 checkpoint skill_heading_hold_goal2_ultratight_hw15speed7):
//   1. re-fit to 64 Hz + the 90 m/s floor, ultra_tight reward, lr 1e-5 -> 3e-5 (several passes)
//   2. bank-limit pass: same reward but bank_soft_limit 0.6109 (35 deg), bank_excess_weight 2.0,
//      lr 3e-5   — raises envelope-wide success to ~1.0 at some cost in heading precision
//   3. this profile (alpha guard on), lr 3e-5 — recovers heading precision and holds the gain
// Pairs with heading_hold_stall_safe.ppo.ron. Full logs:
// target/skill-runs/heading_hold-goal-20260806b/.
//
// Deliberately has NO |roll| penalty term (unlike level_hold's roll_scale/roll_weight):
// bank is the control authority for turning here.
(
    // Heading error term [rad]: -(|heading_error| / heading_error_scale) * heading_error_weight
    heading_error_scale:  0.5,
    heading_error_weight: 1.5,

    // Altitude error term
    alt_error_scale:      60.0,
    alt_error_weight:     1.0,

    // Airspeed error term — tighter speed tracking stabilizes the turn dynamics heading
    // precision depends on (see heading_hold_ultra_tight_tracking.reward.ron's header).
    speed_error_scale:    7.0,
    speed_error_weight:   0.5,

    // Sideslip angle term [rad]
    beta_scale:           0.5,
    beta_weight:          0.15,

    // Roll-RATE term [rad/s] — discourages aileron chatter without penalizing a held bank
    roll_rate_scale:      1.0,
    roll_rate_weight:     0.10,

    // Bank-excess envelope guard (matches the PID heading loop's own +-60 deg clamp, so the
    // BC expert never incurs it). Stage 2 of the recipe above tightens this to 35 deg
    // temporarily; the final stage runs at the standard 60 deg.
    bank_soft_limit:      1.0471975512,  // FRAC_PI_3 = 60 deg
    bank_excess_scale:    0.35,
    bank_excess_weight:   1.0,

    // Angle-of-attack margin guard — ON here (see file header). 0.25 rad = 14.3 deg leaves
    // ~2.3 deg of margin to the airframe's 0.289 rad stall alpha, and the 0.05 rad scale makes
    // sitting *at* the stall cost 1.0/step, comparable to a ~0.5 rad heading error.
    alpha_soft_limit:     0.25,
    alpha_excess_scale:   0.05,
    alpha_excess_weight:  1.0,

    // Constant per-step bonus while alive
    alive_bonus:          0.01,

    // Re-derived for heading_error_weight=1.5 per the discounted-worst-case argument in
    // heading_hold.reward.ron: at gamma=0.99 the horizon is 100 steps and the worst-case
    // per-step heading term is -(pi/0.5)*1.5 ~= -9.42, discounting to ~= -942; -1250.0 keeps
    // the ~1.33x margin. Unchanged from the ultra_tight profile.
    terminal_failure_penalty: -1250.0,

    // Termination conditions
    min_altitude:       10.0,   // [m] crash if below
    max_altitude_error:  500.0, // [m] diverged if |alt - target| exceeds this
    min_airspeed:        60.0,  // [m/s] stall/speed-collapse floor
    max_episode_steps:  3840,   // 60 s @ 64 Hz
)
